  m_Name: Blade19
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Blade (4)
  description: The Blade (4) is responsible for directing the compressed air into
    the combustion chamber, where it mixes with fuel and ignites to produce the high-temperature
    gases that drive the turbine. Its position and shape are carefully designed to
    ensure a smooth, efficient flow of air into the chamber, making it a crucial
    component of the engine's combustion process. Notably, the Blade (4) is often
    made from a high-temperature resistant material, such as ceramic or refractory
    metal, to withstand the extreme conditions encountered in this section.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 8300000, guid: ce5319d4fcc963641acd82f47cf7c9fd, type: 3}
